Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:43:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] jails/instances/lab-claude: Put ~/local/bin on the path
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: pqvspvnxuwnypstqnqzlokqrnqtwtlzl

Tools that run the agent, such as lab-process-mail, are installed as
the claude user under ~/local, so the agent cannot edit the copy that
runs it. Their commands land in ~/local/bin, which was not on the
path, so they could only be run by their full name.

The login class now adds ~/local/bin after the default path, so a
command installed there is found by name, but cannot shadow a system
one.
---
change-id: pqvspvnxuwnypstqnqzlokqrnqtwtlzl

 jails/instances/lab-claude/dist/home/claude/.login_conf | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/jails/instances/lab-claude/dist/home/claude/.login_conf b/jails/instances/lab-claude/dist/home/claude/.login_conf
index f3a0497..8d4e97e 100644
--- a/jails/instances/lab-claude/dist/home/claude/.login_conf
+++ b/jails/instances/lab-claude/dist/home/claude/.login_conf
@@ -8,6 +8,9 @@
 # https://bugs.freebsd.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=298878
 # https://bugs.freebsd.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=299200
 #
+# The path is the default class's plus ~/local/bin, where packages
+# installed as this user with "pkg -r ~/local" put their commands.
+#
 # getcap(3) does not allow comments inside a record, so they all
 # live up here.
 
@@ -29,4 +32,5 @@ me:\
 	CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_PROMPT_SUGGESTION=false,\
 	CLAUDE_CODE_GLOB_NO_IGNORE=false,\
 	CLAUDE_CODE_NATIVE_CURSOR=1,\
-	USE_BUILTIN_RIPGREP=0:
+	USE_BUILTIN_RIPGREP=0:\
+	:path=/sbin /bin /usr/sbin /usr/bin /usr/local/sbin /usr/local/bin ~/bin ~/local/bin:
-- 
